GKE INSTALL (tbd)
===========

Rough manual setup to add BTF to persistent storage for FGS.

(0) Build BTF for image

$ HTTPS_IMAGE = http://launchpadlibrarian.net/442283852/linux-image-unsigned-4.15.0-1044-gke-dbgsym_4.15.0-1044.46_amd64.ddeb
$ pushd ./contrib/vmlinux-builder
$ ./btf-builder.sh $HTTPS_IMAGE
$ popd

(1) Create disk storage

$ gcloud beta compute --project $PROJECT disks create btf-pd \
     --size 1 --type pd-standard                             \
     --replica-zones "us-west1,us-west1"

(2) Apply persistent storage claim

$ pushd ./install/kubernetes/persistVolumes
$ kubectl apply -f hubble-btf-pv.yaml
$ kubectl apply -f hubble-btf-pvc.yaml

(3) Copy BTF to disk

$ gcloud beta compute --project $PROJECT scp --zone "us-west1-a" \
     ~/go/src/github.com/covalentio/hubble-fgs/contrib/vmlinux-builder/btf \
     gke-my-cluster-default-pool-ab1fc632-f7dc:/var/lib/hubble-fgs/btf/

(4) Add mount to hubble.yaml

 - name: hubble-fgs-btf
   mountPath: "/var/lib/hubble-fgs/btf/"

 volumes:
 - name: hubble-fgs-btf
   persistentVolumeClaim:
     claimName: hubble-fgs-btf
